  "losses": [
    "The 593 MiB Qwen2.5-3B embedding is not offered the weight/sparse/patch candidates: TensorPlanOptions::max_delta_bytes defaults to 512 MiB because those encoders hold several full-size copies and cannot run inside 3 GiB. On this corpus the skipped candidates were not the cheapest (the tensor is stored as float-tensor, 413,019,145 B vs raw 622,329,856 B; it was 413,019,145 B on the base pass too).",
    "Mode-9 (float-tensor) encoding is still the single largest transient: the 3B ingest peak is 2,765,636 KiB, and the base+next passes on a 622 MB tensor are the peak.",
    "The stopgap zstd-19 CPU gate skips the embedding at level 19 (estimated 20.8 s > 20 s budget), so the level-19 baseline is not a candidate there.",
    "The full court was run in the reduced configuration only (one family, default config, one rep per phase); the region1/region100 configurations were not re-run for 3B."
  ],
